# Expectation record for 03_initializers/004_designated_array.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 004_designated_array
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Designated array initializers -- sparse, out-of-order, designator-then-positional continuation, implied length, constant-expression designators, row and element designators for a two-dimensional array in both orders, and member and element designators through an array of struct, every slot read back individually at both storage durations; the OVERLAPPING-designator spelling is excluded, narrowly and with its reason recorded in impl_defined_notes, because the frozen warning gate rejects every spelling of it
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
The rule this program has to satisfy that an ordinary initializer program does not is C11 6.7.9p23:
the evaluations of an initializer list's expressions are indeterminately sequenced with respect to
one another, so the order in which their SIDE EFFECTS occur is unspecified. Every initializer
expression here is an integer constant expression -- 1, 10 through 13, 30, 50, 70, 101, 110 through
113, 130, 170, and the small constants in the two-dimensional and struct cases -- and a
constant expression has no side effects at all, so that unspecified order is unobservable. This
matters because several of these forms depend on initializer-list ORDER for their answer:
g_continue resumes positionally after a designator and is then repositioned backwards,
g_row_then_elem and g_elem_then_row spell one aggregate in two orders, and g_st_brace lists its
element braces [2] before [0]. Which slot each initializer lands in is fixed by C11 6.7.9p19,
which initializes in initializer-list order, and that is a separate rule from the sequencing of
side effects that 6.7.9p23 leaves open. Because no initializer expression has a side
effect, there is nothing left for 6.7.9p23 to make unspecified, and no initializer here names a
subobject an earlier one already named, so the one form whose answer would turn on that
distinction is the form this record excludes.
Every designator is in range for its array, and each is a constant expression the compiler resolves
before the program runs: g_sparse is int[8] designated at 7, 3 and 0; g_continue is int[6]
designated at 1 and 0 with the unnamed run 12, 13 continuing at indices 2 and 3, which C11 6.7.9p17
fixes to resume at the element following the designated one; g_constexpr is int[6] designated at
2 + 1, 1 * 2 and 0, which are 3, 2 and 0; the three two-dimensional arrays are int[2][3] designated
within [0..1][0..2]; and the two struct arrays are struct pair[3] designated at 0 and 2.
g_implied has no declared bound, so C11 6.7.9p22 sizes it from its largest designator: its one
designator is [4], making it int[5], and the program reads exactly the length it computes with
sizeof rather than a literal, so a mis-sized array shows up as a wrong g_implied_len line instead of
an out-of-bounds read.
Every subscript in every read loop stays strictly inside its array bound, and each loop bound is
either a literal equal to the declared extent or, for g_implied, the sizeof-derived element count.
No pointer is formed anywhere in the program, so no one-past-the-end pointer exists to be
dereferenced, no pointer arithmetic can leave an object, no address is taken and none is printed.
Every element and member left unmentioned by a designated initializer is initialized to zero by C11
6.7.9p19 and 6.7.9p21 -- a definite value rather than an indeterminate one -- so nothing here reads
uninitialized storage. That applies to the automatic-duration objects exactly as to the static ones,
because an object with any initializer is fully initialized.
No arithmetic is performed on the data, so no signed overflow is reachable. The only arithmetic is
the loop counters' increments, bounded by 8, 6, 5, 4, 2 and 3, and the sizeof quotients, whose
operands are compile-time constants and whose divisor is a sizeof of a complete object type and is
therefore non-zero by the standard's own guarantee. Nothing is shifted and nothing is remaindered.
Nothing is modified after its initialization, so no object is modified twice between two sequence
points.
There is no aliasing violation: every value is read through an lvalue of its own declared type,
which is int in every case, reached by subscripting and member selection only. No object
representation is examined, no union appears in a read, and no cast to a pointer type is present.
The casts in the program are (int) applied to a sizeof quotient whose value is 5 -- a value
conversion that cannot change the number. No padding byte is observed and nothing depends on the
relative addresses of unrelated objects.
Each printf call receives at most two loop counters and one int datum, none of which has a side
effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot be
observed. Every conversion specifier is %d with an argument of type int after the default argument
promotions, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by the
operating system. Nothing outside this file is read: every input is a literal here, no file, socket,
environment variable, clock, random source or locale is consulted, and iteration order is fixed, so
every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a)
while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a
compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h
and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, with no diagnostic of any kind and no
source-level diagnostic suppression anywhere in the translation unit, and it builds and runs clean
under the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched. One initializer spelling is excluded to reach that clean audit rather than suppressed
inside it, and the exclusion, its measured reason and which order-dependent forms remain under test
are recorded in impl_defined_notes below.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing that the harness reads: all four targets, all three optimization
levels and all three oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, no gate
deviation is claimed under the ub_audit_flags key, and no implementation-defined value reaches
this program's output. One initializer SPELLING is nevertheless excluded from the source, and the
paragraph below states which, why, and which order-dependent forms remain under test.
CONSTRAINT-C3 EXCLUSION -- THE OVERLAPPING-DESIGNATOR SPELLING. Overriding a
designated initializer -- naming one subobject twice, so that the LATER initializer supplies
its value -- is well-defined C11 (6.7.9p19, which fixes initialization in initializer-list
order), and getting the order wrong is a realistic compiler defect that stays invisible unless
a program actually overrides something: a front end that folded designators into a map keyed by
index would keep whichever value it happened to insert last, which need not be the one the source
ordered last. GCC nevertheless reports it under -Woverride-init, which -Wextra enables and which
the audit gate's -Werror makes fatal; in this environment `{ [0] = 1, [1] = 2, [0] = 9 }` is
rejected with "initialized field overwritten [-Werror=override-init]". FOURTEEN spellings of an
override were MEASURED against that gate with the reference compiler -- duplicate element
designator, identical-value override, zero-then-value, whole-row brace then element, element then
whole-row brace, that reverse nesting with a later initializer for a different row, positional
continuation running back over an earlier designator, struct-element brace then one member of it,
two member designators then a whole-struct brace, duplicate struct member, two union members, a
nested whole-member brace then one of its members, the reverse of that, and an override inside a
compound literal -- and every one is rejected, so no spelling of that particular route exists that
the unmodified gate accepts. An override carrying a side effect is not an escape either:
-Woverride-init-side-effects is on by DEFAULT and is not a gate member at all, and C11 6.7.9p23
leaves the sequencing of an initializer list's side effects unspecified, which requirement 1
forbids outright -- so the one construction that would have slipped past the diagnostic is barred
by the soundness precondition instead. No admissible deviation exists: the gate's removable
members are exactly -pedantic, for the GCC-extensions area, and -Wconversion with
-Wsign-conversion, for the deliberate narrowing program, so -Wextra is not removable and area 03
is granted no deviation at all. A source-level diagnostic-suppression directive is not an
alternative to that: it neutralizes a gate member from inside the translation unit while this
record still claims the unchanged gate, which would make this record's own claim false rather
than making the program clean. The spelling is therefore dropped from the source, and constraint
C3 is satisfied the way it asks to be -- the exclusion is narrow, it is scoped to one spelling, it
changes no target, no optimization level and no oracle, and its reason is recorded here and in
the program's own header comment. The specific loss is the seven overriding families the file used
to carry, of which the discriminating one was the reverse nesting that separates "the last
initializer to name a subobject wins" from "any explicitly named member survives"; that loss is
stated rather than left to be inferred, and it is a gap in this area that no program closes.
THE ORDERING RULE ITSELF REMAINS UNDER TEST IN THIS PROGRAM, which is what keeps the exclusion
narrow rather than a wholesale retreat from order-dependence. g_continue is
`{ [1] = 11, 12, 13, [0] = 10 }`: a designator, two positional initializers that C11 6.7.9p17
requires to resume at indices 2 and 3, and then a designator that moves the cursor BACKWARDS, so
an implementation that resumed from the wrong place or refused to reposition is caught without any
slot being named twice. g_row_then_elem and g_elem_then_row spell one int[2][3] with a row brace
and an element designator in both orders and must agree. g_elem_only supplies three element
designators out of row order. g_st_brace lists its element braces [2] before [0], and g_st_memb
interleaves member designators across two elements. g_sparse and l_sparse designate descending
indices 7, 3, 0. Every one of those is gate-clean precisely because no initializer in it revisits
a slot an earlier one already named. The bracketed-range designator `[0 ... 3] = 7`, which would
express a repeated fill without an override, is a GCC extension rejected by -Werror=pedantic and
belongs to area 08 rather than here.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Every printed datum is a plain int printed with %d, and the one derived
quantity, g_implied_len, is an element COUNT rather than a size in bytes, so it is 5 on every
target regardless of how wide an int is. No type whose width differs between the ILP32 target and
the three LP64 targets ever reaches a format string: i686 is ELF32 with a four-byte long and
pointer while x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 are ELF64 with eight bytes for both
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462), a difference also MEASURED on all
four targets in this environment, and this program touches neither type. No sizeof result is
printed as a byte count and no _Alignof result is printed at all.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. No character data appears at all, so the MEASURED split -- plain char signed
on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- cannot arise.
PADDING AND LAYOUT. Only named members and elements are read, never an object representation, so no
padding byte is observed; these all-int aggregates carry no internal padding on any of the four
targets in any case. No address is printed, so no layout choice the ABI is free to make is
observable: only the values the initializers supply are.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. Nothing character-valued is printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves nothing here to
the implementation.
THE DISCRIMINATING VARIANT is the pairing of storage durations, which is why all three optimization
levels matter: a static designated initializer is resolved before program startup and emitted into
the data image, whereas the automatic twin's placement is a run-time act the backend performs on
entry to the block, and at a higher level either path may be folded into immediate operands. Every
element of every object is read back individually, so a value landing in the wrong slot, a
disturbed neighbour or a lost zero fill is each its own line, and nothing is summarized.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 70 lines byte-identically
with exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other
without any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. The count is
the mechanically measured length of the golden block below rather than a hand-written figure, and
the same twelve configurations were re-measured after the excluded spelling was removed, so these
70 lines are the current source's output rather than a residue of an earlier one.
END
